Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:02.840
Mind Your Decisions, I'm Presh Talwalkar

00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:08.940
4 ^ x + 6 ^ x = 9 ^ x

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:13.680
Solve for all real values of x that satisfy this equation

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:23.420
I thank Ritwik in India for suggesting this problem

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:23.900
It came from an IIT jee sample paper, but I've also seen it shared on the internet with the catch phrase

00:00:23.949 --> 00:00:25.949
"You should be able to solve this"

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:33.329
Pause the video if you'd like to give this problem a try. And when you're ready keep watching to learn how to solve this problem

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:49.559
We'll get started by dividing each term by 4 to the power of x

00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:52.499
the first term simplifies to be 1

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:56.789
the next term becomes 6 over 4 all raised to the power of x and

00:00:56.890 --> 00:01:00.059
The third term becomes 9 over 4 raised to the power of x

00:01:01.510 --> 00:01:05.460
6 over 4 is equal to 3 over 2 and we'll substitute that in

00:01:06.310 --> 00:01:11.879
9 over 4 is equal to 3 over 2 the quantity squared and we'll substitute that in

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:17.729
We now simplify 3 over 2 squared all raised to the power of x

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:21.509
This becomes 3 over 2 all raised to the power of 2x

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:28.440
now make the substitution that 3 over 2 raised to the power of x is equal to u

00:01:29.229 --> 00:01:35.219
If we square both sides of the equation. We get 3 over 2 all raised to the power of 2x is equal to u squared

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:40.319
We thus have a quadratic equation 1 plus u is equal to u squared

00:01:41.049 --> 00:01:46.828
We'll move the terms to the right hand side. So we get 0 is equal to u squared minus u minus 1

00:01:47.590 --> 00:01:50.820
Since u is equal to 3 over 2 all raised to the power of x

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:56.339
We need u to be greater than 0 because three-halves raised to the power of x will be a positive term

00:01:57.310 --> 00:02:00.359
We then use the quadratic formula and simplify

00:02:00.969 --> 00:02:05.909
We get that u is equal to the golden ratio 1 plus the square root of 5 all over 2

00:02:06.399 --> 00:02:09.599
But we're not done yet. We want to solve for x

00:02:10.780 --> 00:02:14.220
since three-halves raised to the power of x is equal to u

00:02:14.739 --> 00:02:17.999
We want to solve for x by taking the natural log of both sides

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:24.389
We can then bring the exponent down and then solve for x by dividing line the natural log of three-halves

00:02:25.030 --> 00:02:28.320
We substitute in for u and we get our exact answer

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:31.920
x is equal to the natural log of the golden ratio

00:02:32.410 --> 00:02:39.389
divided by the natural log of three-halves and this simplifies to be approximately 1.187

00:02:40.359 --> 00:02:46.889
At first the problem was quite intimidating, but with some clever substitutions, we found the golden answer

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:52.139
Thanks for making Mind Your Decisions one of the best channels on YouTube

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:56.000
As always, thanks for watching and thanks for your support.

